    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-99045",
      "summary": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nibmveth: h_free logical LAN on open-fail after register\n\nibmveth_open() registers the logical LAN, then allocates the RX\nbuffer pools. A pool failure jumps to out_free_buffer_pools without\nh_free_logical_lan(), so PHYP still owns the buffer-list page when\nit is unmapped. request_irq() failure already issued the hypercall\nbefore taking the same label.\n\nMove that h_free to the shared post-register unwind so both paths\nderegister before the buffer list is unmapped.",
      "cvssScore": null,
      "severity": "Unknown",
      "published": "2026-10-23",
      "modified": "2026-10-23",
      "cwe": null,
      "references": [
        "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-99045",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a065bd31ec462f6f9c267026b708dd020f122723",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af0524bf4ce1a4cbd2946aa81751582951cfcab5",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c54bbdf6f0731102a4bf7f5e4ee535b3ea415996",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d24fdec1413c656d29298097926e77542785ca0c"
      ],
      "vulnerableProducts": [],
      "isExploited": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-99066",
      "summary": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: dev: init_can_skb(): restore skb header initialization\n\nCommit 9f10374bb024 (\"can: remove private CAN skb headroom infrastructure\")\nremoved the skb_reset_mac_header()/skb_reset_network_header()/\nskb_reset_transport_header() calls from init_can_skb(). As a result, RX\nskbs from alloc_can_skb() and friends again carry mac_header = 0xFFFF.\nWhen such an skb reaches packet_rcv_spkt() (SOCK_PACKET), the push length\ncalculation overflows and triggers skb_under_panic -> kernel BUG -> full\nmachine panic.\n\nThe same issue was originally reported in 2014 on linux-can and fixed by\ncommit 969439016d2c (\"can: add missing initialisations in CAN related\nskbuffs\"). packet_rcv_spkt() itself has never been hardened: only\npacket_rcv() and tpacket_rcv() gained dev_has_header() checks in\ncommit d549699048b4 (\"net/packet: fix packet receive on L3 devices\nwithout visible hard header\").",
      "cvssScore": null,
      "severity": "Unknown",
      "published": "2026-10-23",
      "modified": "2026-10-23",
      "cwe": null,
      "references": [
        "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-99066",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a04c0cb8606ff88399489d03ef255afe90d0d5f",
        "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8078375dfd0baecd9f1b7b06bb2d6f88d7cb8632"
      ],
      "vulnerableProducts": [],
      "isExploited": false
    },
